{"id": 12696, "url": "https://www.camplife.com/Sauble+Beach+Resort+Camp?newres=y", "read": "2026-10-19", "ref": ["name", "Sauble+Beach+Resort+Camp"], "record": {"images": [{"id": 1543679, "url": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/sunriseimages-prod/static-app-content/cgs/926/images/gallery/1_b.jpg", "contentType": "image", "primary": false, "caption": "", "textSummary": "Campground image 1"}], "campgroundId": 926, "hasOnlineStore": false, "campgroundName": "Sauble Beach Resort Camp", "primaryAddress": {"address1": "877 Main Street", "address2": null, "city": "Sauble Beach", "stateProvince": "ON", "zipCode": "N0H 2G0"}, "phone": "+1 519-422-1101", "email": "info@saubleresortcamp.com", "lat": "44.630522", "lon": "-81.244712", "facebookUrl": null, "twitterId": null, "pinterestUrl": null, "instagramUrl": null, "description": "Welcome to Sauble Beach Resort Camp. We are a well-established and supervised family campground, where we offer 300 available sites for seasonal and overnight camping. We are located just minutes from Sauble Beach, the second-largest freshwater beach in the world, with an 11-kilometer stretch of white sand beach, offering breath-taking sunsets and amazing views of the Lake Huron shoreline!&nbsp;<p><br></p><p>Sauble Beach has been voted the #1 beach in Ontario and is a very popular summer family destination! The Sauble area is also a fisherman’s paradise. In the spring, large rainbow trout can be seen vaulting up the Sauble River Falls and in the summer, lake trout, northern pike, perch, small mouth bass, walleye, and whitefish are in abundance.</p><p><br></p><p>Our facilities include indoor and outdoor pool, hot tub, childrens playground, volleyball, horseshoes, recreation hall, laundry, propane sales, 21 Rental Trailers, and 100 short-term camping sites, some with water, electricity, and sewer. Enforced quite time from 11:00pm to 7:00am, and an on site recreation director.&nbsp;</p><p></p>", "events": "Please refer to our website at, www.saubleresortcamp.c